## The loop

1. **Reproduce** with one command that fails reliably; read the whole first error ([01]({{ref_01}})).
2. **Isolate** — what changed since green, smallest failing case, bisect ([02]({{ref_02}})).
3. **Hypothesize** one cause at a time; check it; log it ([02]({{ref_02}})).
4. **Fix the root cause** at the right layer, smallest change in scope; **regression test** first ([03]({{ref_03}})).
5. **Stop** when it is the environment, when attempts run out, or when the fix changes a contract ([04]({{ref_04}})).
6. **Report** cause, fix, test, evidence, what was ruled out ([06]({{ref_06}})).

## Never

- Edit, skip or weaken a test to make it pass.
- Add fake fallbacks, broad catches, sleeps or retries to hide a failure.
- Loosen types/assertions or disable lint/gates.
- Change code to work around a broken environment, or touch a stack you did not start.
- Leave debug output behind.

